{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.GoldenQuartetGalois","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.GoldenQuartetGalois","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.golden_quartet_galois","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.golden_quartet_galois","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L123-L139","doc":"**Golden quartet as Galois × bar orbit** (Proposition):\n\nThe four values {1/φ, −φ, φ, −1/φ} are the complete root set of\nP(x) = x⁴ − 3x² + 1, with Galois action (√5 ↔ −√5) producing the\nsign flips on each minimal polynomial, and bar (x ↔ x⁻¹) exchanging\nthe two minimal polynomials.\n\nThe conjunction below records the four roots and the bar pairing. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:golden-quartet-galois","label":"prop:golden-quartet-galois","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.galois_phiInv_eq_neg_phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.galois_phiInv_eq_neg_phi","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L116-L121","doc":"The Galois conjugate of 1/φ in ℚ(√5)/ℚ is −φ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.galois_phi_eq_neg_phiInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.galois_phi_eq_neg_phiInv","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L107-L114","doc":"The Galois conjugate of φ in ℚ(√5)/ℚ is −1/φ.\nSpecifically, replacing √5 with −√5 in the formula for φ\ngives −1/φ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phi_mul_phiInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phi_mul_phiInv","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L100-L105","doc":"φ · (1/φ) = 1 (bar pairing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.neg_phiInv_quartic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.neg_phiInv_quartic","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L94-L98","doc":"−1/φ satisfies P(x) = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.neg_phi_quartic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.neg_phi_quartic","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L87-L92","doc":"−φ satisfies P(x) = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phiInv_quartic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phiInv_quartic","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L77-L85","doc":"1/φ satisfies P(x) = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phi_quartic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phi_quartic","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L67-L75","doc":"All four golden quartet values satisfy P(x) = x⁴ − 3x² + 1 = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.neg_phiInv_root_pos_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.neg_phiInv_root_pos_sign","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L61-L65","doc":"−1/φ is a root of x² − x − 1 (the same minimal polynomial as φ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.neg_phi_root_neg_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.neg_phi_root_neg_sign","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L55-L59","doc":"−φ is a root of x² + x − 1 (the same minimal polynomial as 1/φ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phiInv_root_neg_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phiInv_root_neg_sign","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L48-L53","doc":"1/φ is a root of x² + x − 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phi_root_pos_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phi_root_pos_sign","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L41-L46","doc":"φ is a root of x² − x − 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.quartic_factorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.quartic_factorisation","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L31-L36","doc":"The quartic factorisation P(x) = (x² − x − 1)(x² + x − 1)\n= x⁴ − 3x² + 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phiInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phiInv","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L28-L29","doc":"1/φ = (√5 − 1)/2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GoldenQuartetGalois.phi","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/golden-quartet-galois.lean#L25-L26","doc":"φ = (1 + √5)/2. ","signatureChunk":0}]}